WEBVTT

00:04.540 --> 00:07.920
This is pretty difficult.

00:07.920 --> 00:09.230
Is this right?

00:10.760 --> 00:13.020
Yes! That should be good!

00:13.020 --> 00:15.740
Yours looks awfully big though?

00:15.740 --> 00:17.650
Huh? Is it?

00:18.630 --> 00:22.330
Are you making snacks for Shido and the others?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.780
Yeah, that's right!

00:24.780 --> 00:30.380
Mhmm. Right now, Master and the others 
are preparing for the coming battle.

00:30.380 --> 00:33.440
Wracking their brains is sure 
to make them hungry.

00:33.440 --> 00:35.340
Yoshino, Natsumi, would you like 
to make some too?

00:35.340 --> 00:36.850
It's fun!

00:36.850 --> 00:37.910
Huh?

00:37.910 --> 00:41.440
N-No I wouldn't...

00:41.440 --> 00:42.820
Please let us help.

00:42.820 --> 00:45.600
We want to be helpful to everyone.

00:46.990 --> 00:50.060
Yoshinon's pads spout fire.

00:50.060 --> 00:50.660
Huh?

00:50.660 --> 00:53.330
You say a bunny doesn't have pads?

00:54.500 --> 00:57.740
I hate clever brats like you.

00:57.740 --> 00:59.760
Natsumi, you should join us, too.

00:59.760 --> 01:02.370
I'm sure it'll be fun to do together.

01:02.720 --> 01:05.870
Huh? But, u-umm...

01:05.870 --> 01:07.660
Yes, yes, it's settled now.

01:07.660 --> 01:09.380
Hurry up and get walking.

01:09.380 --> 01:10.940
Come on, come on.

02:44.520 --> 02:48.500
From far and wide, 
non-erotic words that sound erotic!

02:49.270 --> 02:50.390
Cockle!

02:50.660 --> 02:54.020
Well... Bountiful.

02:54.020 --> 02:56.530
Answer, sacks.

02:56.530 --> 02:57.450
Huh?

02:57.450 --> 03:00.370
Uhh, umm...

03:00.370 --> 03:02.660
Machu Picchu?

03:02.660 --> 03:05.640
Huh? Tell us a bit more about that, Kaguya!

03:05.640 --> 03:08.020
How is Machu Picchu erotic?

03:08.020 --> 03:10.140
I want to know too!

03:10.140 --> 03:11.840
Please, inform us!

03:11.840 --> 03:14.290
Demand. I seek an explanation.

03:14.580 --> 03:19.170
What do you find sexually arousing 
about a ruin of the Inca Empire?

03:19.170 --> 03:23.060
Wh-Why are you only probing into my answer?!

03:25.900 --> 03:29.800
Umm, because it sounds like...

03:29.800 --> 03:31.300
Huh? Sounds like what?

03:31.300 --> 03:33.140
I can't understand at all!

03:33.140 --> 03:36.070
Explain. Please provide more detail.

03:37.940 --> 03:41.320
I-It sounds like the sounds a kiss makes.

03:44.580 --> 03:46.330
That's why?

03:46.330 --> 03:49.280
Man, you're so cute, Kaguya-san.

03:49.280 --> 03:50.400
Mercy.

03:50.400 --> 03:52.520
Well, you seem to genuinely mean that,

03:52.520 --> 03:54.130
so I'll accept it.

03:54.130 --> 03:56.800
What are you being so evasive about?

03:56.800 --> 03:58.580
All of you should explain yours, as well!

03:58.580 --> 04:00.590
What's erotic about "cockles"?

04:00.590 --> 04:02.420
Huh? It's close to co-

04:02.420 --> 04:05.080
Ahh, could you please not explain!

04:05.080 --> 04:08.880
Huh? After you told us all to explain?

04:08.880 --> 04:10.100
Well, whatever.

04:10.100 --> 04:11.960
Then let's continue.

04:11.960 --> 04:13.310
Chincilla.

04:13.310 --> 04:16.500
Uhh... "Bust".

04:16.500 --> 04:18.610
Answer, six.

04:20.050 --> 04:22.490
Ch-Chupacabra.

04:23.810 --> 04:25.520
How is that erotic?!

04:25.520 --> 04:27.080
Please tell us!

04:27.080 --> 04:28.050
Confusion.

04:28.050 --> 04:31.750
What aspect of a blood-sucking UMA from 
South America brings you sexual arousal?

04:31.750 --> 04:34.780
I don't want to play with you
guys any more!

04:34.780 --> 04:36.700
Huh? Oh!

04:36.700 --> 04:41.060
Then, from far and wide, 
scenes where that boy was cool.

04:41.060 --> 04:41.590
Huh?

04:41.590 --> 04:43.410
For me,

04:43.410 --> 04:47.960
I think it has to be when he refused to give up 
on kissing me even when I was nearly dead.

04:47.960 --> 04:50.410
He held me tight and went for it!

04:50.410 --> 04:52.000
For me it was that one time.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.650
The moment he risked his own life

04:53.650 --> 04:58.550
to protect me from Inverted Tohka's 
attack in the DEM Japan Branch.

04:59.270 --> 05:01.940
Just remembering it reminds me how cool he was!

05:02.300 --> 05:03.450
Proposal.

05:03.450 --> 05:07.520
It was the time when he stopped me 
and Kaguya from fighting.

05:07.520 --> 05:08.800
Oh, not fair!

05:08.800 --> 05:10.620
That's the one I was about to say!

05:12.910 --> 05:16.090
We don't want to let that boy die, do we?

05:16.090 --> 05:17.930
If it weren't for Darling,

05:17.930 --> 05:22.250
I probably wouldn't be able 
to trust anyone still.

05:22.250 --> 05:23.330
Affirmative.

05:23.330 --> 05:25.000
If not for Shido,

05:25.000 --> 05:29.140
only Kaguya or I would exist 
in this world, not both.

05:29.530 --> 05:33.770
I would definitely be dead 
if it wasn't for that boy.

05:43.150 --> 05:45.030
Tohka
Cell Phone

05:43.410 --> 05:45.260
Hmm, Tohka?

05:45.030 --> 05:45.650
Call In Progress

05:46.570 --> 05:47.880
<i>Kaguya?!</i>

05:47.880 --> 05:50.960
<i>We're making snacks for Shido 
and the others right now,</i>

05:50.960 --> 05:52.160
<i>but would you like to join us?</i>

05:52.560 --> 05:55.420
<i>U-Umm, Yoshino here.</i>

05:55.420 --> 05:56.650
<i>Yuzuru,</i>

05:56.650 --> 06:00.420
<i>we're making snacks for Shido 
and the others right now, but...</i>

06:00.740 --> 06:01.840
<i>Nia?</i>

06:01.840 --> 06:03.010
<i>It's Muku.</i>

06:03.010 --> 06:04.300
<i>Come lend us a hand.</i>

06:04.300 --> 06:06.300
Sunday, February 18th

06:04.300 --> 06:06.300
<b>Natsumi</b>

06:04.300 --> 06:06.300
Help us make snacks

06:06.800 --> 06:11.970
Ah! Natsumi, why are you the only one 
to text instead of calling?!

06:11.970 --> 06:15.070
Please let me hear your cute voice!

06:17.730 --> 06:20.690
Shizaki, how's our requests for aid 
to each branch going?

06:21.100 --> 06:21.980
All sent.

06:22.630 --> 06:24.940
I'll report once I have replies from each.

06:25.220 --> 06:27.570
MARIA, have we finished 
maintenance on our units?

06:27.860 --> 06:30.940
There's essentially no issue, 
but if I may be greedy,

06:30.940 --> 06:34.440
I would like the Wizards to conduct 
a manual inspection of the basic Realizers.

06:34.440 --> 06:38.580
Also, I would like to request a wash 
and wax for my outer plating.

06:38.890 --> 06:42.040
We'll do something about the former, 
but the latter is denied.

06:42.040 --> 06:44.810
You're going to get disgustingly filthy 
two days from now anyways.

06:46.070 --> 06:49.370
In women, the heart is 
the first thing to wane, Kotori.

06:49.370 --> 06:50.590
What was that?!

06:50.960 --> 06:52.650
Calm down, Kotori.

06:53.450 --> 06:55.250
Why don't you take a break?

06:55.250 --> 06:57.520
Thanks, I'll take it.

06:57.520 --> 06:58.700
Sorry.

06:58.700 --> 07:01.350
I wish there was something I could do, too.

07:01.820 --> 07:03.380
What are you talking about?

07:03.380 --> 07:06.760
I'm going to be assigning you 
the toughest mission,

07:06.760 --> 07:09.240
so you won't have the leeway to aid others.

07:09.590 --> 07:11.110
Toughest mission?

07:11.500 --> 07:14.110
Survive, no matter what.

07:16.370 --> 07:17.610
I see.

07:17.610 --> 07:19.100
You're certainly right about that.

07:19.850 --> 07:23.020
Both DEM and Kurumi are targeting you.

07:23.020 --> 07:25.850
I'm also worried about how Phantom will act.

07:27.380 --> 07:29.810
Especially since we don't know 
Phantom's identity

07:29.810 --> 07:32.540
or what her goal behind making more Spirits is.

07:32.540 --> 07:35.450
I can't help getting an ominous 
feeling about that.

07:36.260 --> 07:38.390
Phantom's goal, huh?

07:38.810 --> 07:42.610
It might be something surprisingly silly.

07:42.610 --> 07:43.400
Huh?

07:45.930 --> 07:47.160
Snack time!

07:47.160 --> 07:49.260
We made onigiri.

07:50.270 --> 07:52.280
Eat to your heart's content.

07:52.490 --> 07:54.410
<b>Kotori</b>

07:52.580 --> 07:54.410
These are yours, Kotori!

07:54.820 --> 07:58.040
Wow. Are there different ingredients inside?

07:58.300 --> 08:00.090
Thank you.

08:02.970 --> 08:03.980
Kotori?

08:03.980 --> 08:04.920
What's wrong?

08:07.420 --> 08:08.920
Cilantro?!

08:08.920 --> 08:10.560
What is this, bullying?

08:10.560 --> 08:13.010
You know I hate cilantro, right?!

08:13.360 --> 08:17.960
We wanted to strengthen 
our minds to help defeat DEM,

08:17.960 --> 08:20.770
so we decided to try conquering our dislikes.

08:20.770 --> 08:24.520
Even our own onigiri are filled 
with things we don't like.

08:27.230 --> 08:29.420
My onigiri has umeboshi!

08:31.990 --> 08:33.870
Mine has pickled wasabi!

08:34.780 --> 08:37.170
M-Mine has celery...

08:42.370 --> 08:43.270
Go on!

08:44.310 --> 08:46.680
You should overcome this trial, too, Shido!

08:46.680 --> 08:47.390
Huh?

08:49.250 --> 08:52.760
<b>Shido</b>

08:49.780 --> 08:52.460
What... is in mine?

08:54.070 --> 08:56.180
We really debated on your onigiri.

08:56.180 --> 08:59.730
After all, there aren't many foods you dislike.

08:59.730 --> 09:00.850
Affirmative.

09:00.850 --> 09:03.770
Yours went through careful 
consideration until the very end.

09:04.710 --> 09:08.810
Darling, if you have trouble eating it, 
then I'll help you!

09:08.810 --> 09:11.750
S-So what is in mine, then?

09:16.190 --> 09:19.790
At least tell me what you put inside it!

09:27.750 --> 09:28.540
Shido?

09:30.150 --> 09:32.390
Tohka, what's wrong?

09:32.390 --> 09:33.670
Can't sleep?

09:34.370 --> 09:35.310
Yeah.

09:35.670 --> 09:38.300
Miku has awful sleeping habits.

09:38.730 --> 09:41.260
She crawled over the floor like a caterpillar

09:41.260 --> 09:44.500
and tried to sneak into my bed.

09:46.890 --> 09:49.350
Was she really asleep, then?

09:49.720 --> 09:51.660
What about you, Shido?

09:52.130 --> 09:56.010
Yeah, I was thinking about Kurumi for a bit.

09:57.330 --> 10:00.750
I will... make sure to save Kurumi.

10:01.250 --> 10:02.850
I'll seal away her Spirit Power

10:02.850 --> 10:05.410
and make her atone for her sins as best I could.

10:06.090 --> 10:07.250
That's what I used to think.

10:09.460 --> 10:13.990
But is what I consider salvation 
truly salvation for Kurumi?

10:13.990 --> 10:15.270
I don't know.

10:16.170 --> 10:18.710
Kurumi is trying to save her best friend.

10:19.380 --> 10:23.230
Is making her give up on that 
really saving her?

10:26.000 --> 10:28.820
I have to save Kurumi, no matter what.

10:29.630 --> 10:32.330
But what should I be doing to achieve that?

10:33.240 --> 10:35.710
What can I do for her?

10:37.550 --> 10:39.780
Can I sit next to you?

10:40.180 --> 10:41.910
Yeah, of course.

10:43.700 --> 10:45.070
Huh? Huh?!

10:47.980 --> 10:50.890
They did this on the TV's <i>With Mother</i> show.

10:51.590 --> 10:54.390
Apparently it helps relax the mind.

10:57.580 --> 10:59.770
Thank you, Tohka.

11:00.450 --> 11:03.090
You're always helping me so much.

11:04.590 --> 11:06.210
That's not true.

11:06.690 --> 11:09.810
I have to apologize to you, Shido.

11:10.090 --> 11:10.820
Huh?

11:11.490 --> 11:17.440
When I heard that you would have 
died if not for Kurumi,

11:17.900 --> 11:21.550
I felt my chest tightening up.

11:22.590 --> 11:24.790
Then I thought to myself,

11:25.690 --> 11:30.050
"If I hadn't met Shido back then,

11:30.050 --> 11:33.590
then Shido wouldn't have to face that."

11:34.380 --> 11:39.460
Even now, you wouldn't be 
stressing yourself this much.

11:44.030 --> 11:44.970
Tohka.

11:46.220 --> 11:48.100
What are you saying?

11:48.100 --> 11:52.230
I'm truly happy that I met you that day.

11:52.970 --> 11:54.100
But...

11:54.640 --> 11:56.900
Sure I've faced danger, too,

11:57.380 --> 12:02.610
but I've received so much 
from you and all the Spirits.

12:03.110 --> 12:08.730
Even if I could go back to our meeting 
with all the memories I have now,

12:08.730 --> 12:12.190
I would still reach out to you 
without any hesitation.

12:13.310 --> 12:14.460
Shido...

12:36.450 --> 12:38.270
Good morning, everyone!

12:38.570 --> 12:40.280
What great weather we have today, huh?

12:40.280 --> 12:41.680
Morning, Tonomochi.

12:41.680 --> 12:43.610
Wait, it's cloudy today.

12:43.610 --> 12:46.530
Hey, have you heard anything from Itsuka?

12:46.530 --> 12:49.530
No. He probably still has that cold.

12:50.030 --> 12:52.060
But it's odd, isn't it?

12:52.060 --> 12:54.520
Tokisaki has been absent the whole time, too.

12:54.520 --> 12:55.880
That's so lame.

12:55.880 --> 12:58.170
So have Tohka and Tobiichi, right?

12:58.570 --> 13:02.670
You don't think they're being seduced 
by sex-fiend Itsuka, do you?

13:02.670 --> 13:05.420
Maybe all four of them 
are on a hot springs trip!

13:05.420 --> 13:06.900
That's so lame.

13:07.990 --> 13:11.660
Come on, Itsuka of all people would never—

13:11.660 --> 13:12.810
Do that?

13:13.310 --> 13:16.050
No, it's plenty possible.

13:16.050 --> 13:17.690
I'll tell you if I find anything out.

13:18.150 --> 13:20.340
Thank you for your cooperation.

13:21.970 --> 13:23.380
A spacequake?!

13:23.380 --> 13:24.720
No way. Again?

13:24.720 --> 13:26.020
That's so lame.

13:26.020 --> 13:28.240
Come on, let's go to the school's shelter.

13:28.240 --> 13:29.220
Yeah!

13:29.220 --> 13:30.200
Hmm?

13:31.950 --> 13:33.840
What's wrong, Tonomachi?

13:33.840 --> 13:37.480
Well, did you see anything just now?

13:37.480 --> 13:38.460
In the sky?

13:38.460 --> 13:40.100
You saw something?

13:40.100 --> 13:44.710
Hmm, it kind of looked like a battleship?

13:46.410 --> 13:49.450
Tonomachi, have you finally damaged your brain?

13:49.450 --> 13:53.250
No, he's become one of the boys 
"who can see special things".

13:53.250 --> 13:54.470
That's so lame.

13:54.990 --> 13:58.650
Could you at least say those things 
where I can't hear them?

14:01.920 --> 14:05.040
That's strange, I know-

14:05.040 --> 14:06.190
Tonomachi,

14:06.610 --> 14:07.860
we're leaving you behind!

14:08.170 --> 14:11.240
Ah, wait up for me!

14:12.500 --> 14:14.450
The DEM fleet has emerged.

14:14.970 --> 14:17.000
Their fleet numbers roughly thirty ships!

14:17.510 --> 14:20.450
That's nearly every ship DEM possesses.

14:21.100 --> 14:23.250
Looks like our intel was accurate.

14:23.620 --> 14:25.210
How's the city?

14:25.210 --> 14:27.260
Residents have completed evacuation.

14:27.540 --> 14:29.260
There's no one on the surface.

14:29.740 --> 14:33.010
Good. Now we can fight without holding back.

14:33.740 --> 14:36.520
<i>This is Fraxinus Commander, Kotori Itsuka.</i>

14:37.000 --> 14:40.150
<i>First, I'm truly grateful 
for all your cooperation.</i>

14:40.510 --> 14:44.150
<i>An insolent visitor has arrived in our city.</i>

14:44.500 --> 14:46.610
<i>They're the lowest, 
scummiest kind of abusive man</i>

14:46.610 --> 14:50.910
<i>who tries to steal the power of Spirits 
through rough and violent means!</i>

14:51.290 --> 14:54.990
Yeah. Hate it, right? Well beyond deplorable.

14:54.990 --> 14:59.220
<i>Men who try to dominate 
women through force like that</i>

14:59.220 --> 15:01.890
<i>are always the kind who cowardly 
cling to them when abandoned.</i>

15:02.490 --> 15:06.760
Now! Let's teach these 
ill-mannered thugs a lesson!

15:07.060 --> 15:09.670
Teach them the proper way to treat women.

15:09.670 --> 15:12.170
Teach them how to elegantly escort a woman.

15:12.170 --> 15:14.770
Teach them how we conduct our dates!

15:14.770 --> 15:15.710
Roger!

15:16.010 --> 15:17.520
Yeah!

15:17.780 --> 15:19.640
What incredible fervor.

15:20.020 --> 15:22.650
Yeah, Kotori was cool, too!

15:23.100 --> 15:27.400
It is the commander's job 
to raise everyone's morale.

15:27.780 --> 15:32.560
Though we only have six ships 
against our enemy's aerial fleet of 30.

15:32.560 --> 15:35.730
On top of that, they have several 
thousand Bandersnatch, too.

15:36.300 --> 15:40.370
Plus we have no idea 
how many Nibeelcole will pop up.

15:40.370 --> 15:45.290
But you Spirits are the key 
to overcoming this situation.

15:45.850 --> 15:50.080
I know it might be wrong for the leader of 
an organization dedicated to protecting Spirits

15:50.080 --> 15:52.300
to ask those very same Spirits for their help,

15:52.690 --> 15:54.020
but please.

15:54.020 --> 15:55.630
Please lend us your power.

15:56.030 --> 15:59.060
I ask you as the commander of Ratatoskr, no,

15:59.360 --> 16:03.810
I ask you as Shido's little sister, 
please save my older brother!

16:04.500 --> 16:05.560
Of course!

16:06.110 --> 16:09.330
Please let us help, too.

16:09.330 --> 16:10.850
That's right!

16:10.850 --> 16:14.200
In fact, we'd be angry 
if you tried to leave us out!

16:14.200 --> 16:17.590
Raising morale is a commander's job?

16:18.870 --> 16:22.460
Then you're quite 
the commander now, little sister!

16:22.460 --> 16:26.460
Yes. Kotori is the only commander 
who can lead us!

16:26.460 --> 16:27.500
Affirmative.

16:27.500 --> 16:30.840
I'm willing to place 
our lives in Kotori's hands.

16:35.820 --> 16:36.850
Everyone...

16:38.820 --> 16:42.810
Nia, it's okay to hold a strategy 
meeting here now, right?

16:43.220 --> 16:47.400
Yeah. I'm jamming Beelzebub.

16:47.400 --> 16:51.140
Even if he tries to peek at our 
situation now, he won't make it in time.

16:52.190 --> 16:54.820
So, what evil plots do you have?

16:55.170 --> 16:58.980
Proposal. Why don't we use Mukuro's Michael

16:58.980 --> 17:02.360
to link spaces and storm 
the enemy's command center?

17:02.360 --> 17:05.210
Ah, I knew we were thinking the same thing!

17:05.210 --> 17:07.460
I just didn't say it because 
we couldn't speak it out loud.

17:08.020 --> 17:11.500
Sorry, but that might be impossible.

17:11.500 --> 17:14.170
Ever since Master sealed away my Spirit Power,

17:14.170 --> 17:16.590
I've had difficulty 
with long-range teleportation.

17:16.590 --> 17:19.220
Even if it were possible, I wouldn't permit it.

17:19.220 --> 17:21.640
Our enemy is naturally wary of that,

17:21.640 --> 17:24.680
and we have no idea 
what kind of traps they've set for it.

17:24.680 --> 17:31.250
The Bandersnatch are being operated 
by DEM's new Realizers, Ashcroft β.

17:31.770 --> 17:35.860
They were created using 
Artemisia Ashcroft's brain as their model.

17:35.860 --> 17:37.500
What did you say?

17:37.500 --> 17:39.570
Artemisia?

17:40.020 --> 17:42.240
Wait, the Wizard that was with Ellen?

17:42.240 --> 17:46.000
She was originally the ace 
of Britain's Anti-Spirit Team.

17:46.000 --> 17:50.410
DEM succeeded in integrating 
a control function into the Realizers

17:50.410 --> 17:53.880
after tracing her brain.

17:54.340 --> 17:59.260
MARIA, if we captured her, 
would it be possible for you

17:59.260 --> 18:02.640
to use her brainwave data to create 
a jamming code for the Ashcroft β?

18:03.030 --> 18:05.390
Yes. It would likely be possible.

18:05.890 --> 18:09.890
She was always skeptical 
about the way DEM does things.

18:09.890 --> 18:15.400
And now I think she's only obeying DEM 
because they've manipulated her memories.

18:15.680 --> 18:17.160
If we push there,

18:17.160 --> 18:21.030
I think we have a good chance of capturing her.

18:21.400 --> 18:24.020
I see. Got it.

18:24.020 --> 18:27.290
MARIA, you sounded like you had a strategy, too?

18:27.290 --> 18:28.540
Yes.

18:28.540 --> 18:31.460
There is a way to render 
the Nibeelcole powerless.

18:31.460 --> 18:33.200
Though to do so,

18:33.200 --> 18:36.050
we'll need to have Shido on the front lines.

18:36.050 --> 18:37.340
You need Shido?

18:37.340 --> 18:39.890
You know I can't ever permit that!

18:39.890 --> 18:42.680
This battle is all about protecting Shido!

18:43.090 --> 18:43.900
Yes.

18:43.900 --> 18:48.690
However, we cannot win if we 
don't do something about the Nibeelcole.

18:49.150 --> 18:51.360
But still...

18:51.360 --> 18:53.060
No, let's do it.

18:53.060 --> 18:54.940
Let me hear your plan, MARIA.

18:55.450 --> 18:56.710
Shido...

18:58.670 --> 19:00.120
All right.

19:00.120 --> 19:03.320
But before that, let's go show them

19:03.640 --> 19:08.890
just what it means to fight us in this city!

19:16.540 --> 19:21.590
It would seem Nightmare 
passed along my message.

19:22.070 --> 19:26.000
It looks like Ratatoskr 
is deploying all their forces, too.

19:26.000 --> 19:28.020
Wise decision.

19:28.020 --> 19:31.230
They have no chance of winning 
if they don't take the offensive here.

19:31.770 --> 19:36.750
They're most likely intending 
to come after my head and yours.

19:37.230 --> 19:43.110
It's well known that DEM 
would collapse if it lost us.

19:43.500 --> 19:48.180
In that case, Ike, 
shouldn't you be in a safer location?

19:48.660 --> 19:52.120
We started this revolution.

19:52.440 --> 19:57.170
So I can't allow you to be 
the only one standing at its front.

19:59.550 --> 20:03.050
Now, shall we begin, Captain?

20:03.050 --> 20:03.760
Yes, sir!

20:04.220 --> 20:08.010
All ships, launch the first wave 
of Bandersnatch!

20:18.360 --> 20:20.200
Magic cannons, prepare to fire!

20:20.200 --> 20:22.850
Target Ratatoskr's aerial battleship!

20:24.950 --> 20:26.840
An attack from Ratatoskr?!

20:26.840 --> 20:28.780
It's not! This is—!

20:43.190 --> 20:45.930
Attention, please.

20:45.930 --> 20:50.270
Can you hear me, vile Wizards?

20:50.570 --> 20:51.890
Nightmare!

20:52.290 --> 20:57.010
<i>Starting now, I'm coming to hunt you all down.</i>

20:57.010 --> 20:59.840
<i>Do please try not to flee.</i>

20:59.840 --> 21:00.850
What?!

21:02.530 --> 21:07.550
Ship 2, Honorius! Ship 3, Notoria! 
Cover the Bandersnatch squad!

21:11.370 --> 21:13.000
What?! What happened?!

21:13.000 --> 21:15.290
It looks like we've been hit 
with cannons from the surface!

21:15.290 --> 21:16.860
From the surface?

21:34.060 --> 21:37.180
What is going on with this city?!

21:37.180 --> 21:39.060
Let's accept their challenge.

21:40.790 --> 21:43.200
All we need do is remain calm

21:43.200 --> 21:47.490
and lower our fist with full force.

21:51.080 --> 21:55.000
<b>Episode 2</b>

21:51.080 --> 21:55.000
<b>Final Respite</b>

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
Episode 3   "The Spirit's Resurrection"

23:26.000 --> 23:28.650
And so the battle has begun.

23:29.090 --> 23:32.340
What is the new combat strategy 
Shido employs against Nibeelcole?

23:33.140 --> 23:35.850
Next Episode is Episode 3: 
"The Spirit's Resurrection."

23:36.140 --> 23:39.270
The most powerful Spirit now manifests itself.
